<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thubten Gyatso</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1933</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as 13th Dalai Lama</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thubten Gyatso was the 13th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a>. He fled the British invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> in 1904 and a Qing army in 1910, but returned after the Qing collapse and in 1913 proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>'s independence. He then attempted to modernise Tibet's army, postal service and currency, though monastic opposition limited his reforms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thubten-gyatso.jpg" alt="Thubten Gyatso" width="320" height="412" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M. Sain, Darjeeling · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:13thDalaiLama1910.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
